'''Z.AI Co., Ltd.''',<ref>{{cite web |url=https://ea-cdn.eurolandir.com/press-releases-attachments./4153816/HKEX-EPS_20260714_12244164_0.PDF |title=CHANGE OF THE ENGLISH NAME OF THE COMPANY AND ENGLISH STOCK SHORT NAME |date=14 July 2026 |accessdate=2026-07-23 }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Z.AI CO., LTD. - H SHARES (2513) |url=https://www.hkex.com.hk/Market-Data/Securities-Prices/Equities/Equities-Quote?sym=2513&sc_lang=en |access-date=2026-07-23 |website=[[Hong Kong Stock Exchange]]}}</ref>{{efn|formerly as Beijing Zhipu Huazhang Technology Co., Ltd. ({{lang-zh|s=北京智谱华章科技有限公司}}) and Knowledge Atlas Technology Joint Stock Co., Ltd.}} branded internationally as '''Z.ai''',<ref name=":9" /><ref>{{Cite web |last=Wolf |first=Nate |title=Zhipu AI Stock Rises After Hong Kong IPO as More Chinese AI Offerings Line Up |url=https://www.barrons.com/articles/zhipu-ai-hong-kong-ipo-china-minimax-9afc9f02 |access-date=2026-02-10 |website=[[Barron's]] |language=en-us |quote=Also known as Z.ai, the company describes itself as China’s largest independent large language model developer.}}</ref> is a [[Artificial intelligence industry in China|Chinese artificial intelligence]] company; their flagship product is the [[GLM (AI)|GLM]] (General Language Model) family of [[open weights]] [[Large language model|large language models]] (LLMs). Formerly known as '''Zhipu AI''' outside China until 2025,<ref name=":5" /><ref name=":2" /><ref name=":9" /> it is China's first major LLM company to make [[initial public offering]], on the [[Hong Kong Stock Exchange]] in January 2026.<ref name=":14" /> With a [[market capitalization]] of US$62 billion as of August 2026, it is the most valuable public AI [[pure play]] in China.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Companies ranked by Market Cap - CompaniesMarketCap.com |url=https://companiesmarketcap.com/ |access-date=2026-08-29 |website=companiesmarketcap.com |language=en-US}}</ref>

Founded in [[Beijing]] in 2019 by [[Jie Tang]] as a [[Tsinghua University]] [[Corporate spin-off|spin-out]], researchers introduced the first GLM version in May 2022, preceding the [[AI boom]]. Z.ai's models have released under the [[free and open-source]] [[MIT License]] since July 2025; they have also released [[Vision language model|vision language models]], [[Text-to-video model|text-to-video models]], and the ZCode [[AI-assisted software development|AI coding harness]].

As of 2024, it is one of China's six "[[AI tiger]]" companies<ref>{{Cite web |date=10 March 2025 |title=Meet the 'Six Tigers' that dominate China's AI industry |url=https://qz.com/china-six-tigers-ai-startup-zhipu-moonshot-minimax-01ai-1851768509 |access-date=2025-09-13 |website=Quartz }}</ref> by investors and considered to be the third-largest LLM market player in China according to the [[International Data Corporation]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=22 August 2024 |title=Baidu, SenseTime lead China's market for business-focused LLMs, says IDC |url=https://www.scmp.com/tech/tech-trends/article/3275475/baidu-sensetime-lead-chinas-market-business-focused-large-language-models-says-idc |access-date=24 August 2024 |website=South China Morning Post }}</ref> In January 2025, the [[United States Department of Commerce|United States Commerce Department]] blacklisted the company in its [[Entity List]] due to national security concerns.<ref name=":6" /> Z.ai owns [[AMiner (database)|AMiner]], a research database similar to [[Google Scholar]].

== Name ==
The company's full name within China is {{Langx|zh|北京智谱华章科技有限公司|Běijīng Zhìpǔ Huázhāng Kējì Yǒuxiàn Gōngsī|Beijing Zhipu Huazhang Technology Co., Ltd.|label=none}} The term Zhipu was sometimes translated by Chinese researchers as 'Wisdom Spectrum'.<ref>{{Cite journal |last=Qian |first=Pengbo |last2=Xie |first2=Xingzheng |date=1 February 2026 |title=Task–Technology Fit Leads to Conflict: The Double-Edged-Sword Effect of Generative Artificial Intelligence on Scientific Creative Performance in Humanities and Social Sciences Research |url=https://doi.org/10.1080/10447318.2025.2526580 |journal=International Journal of Human–Computer Interaction |volume=42 |issue=3 |pages=1867–1891 |doi=10.1080/10447318.2025.2526580 |issn=1044-7318|url-access=subscription }}</ref><ref>{{Cite journal |last=Li |first=Qingxu |last2=Chen |first2=Jindong |last3=Zhang |first3=Wen |date=2025 |editor-last=Tang |editor-first=Xijin |editor2-last=Huynh |editor2-first=Van Nam |editor3-last=Xia |editor3-first=Haoxiang |editor4-last=Bai |editor4-first=Quan |title=Data Augmentation Using Large Language Model for Fake Review Identification |url=https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-981-96-0178-3_16 |journal=Knowledge and Systems Sciences |location=Singapore |publisher=Springer Nature |pages=225–238 |doi=10.1007/978-981-96-0178-3_16 |isbn=978-981-96-0178-3|url-access=subscription }}</ref><ref>{{Cite journal |last=Li |first=Hongmei |last2=Liu |first2=Yan |date=2025 |editor-last=Schrepp |editor-first=Martin |title=Study on the Enhancement of Artistic Quality of Community Public Spaces Enabled by AIGC Technology |url=https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-93227-4_4 |journal=Design, User Experience, and Usability |location=Cham |publisher=Springer Nature Switzerland |pages=47–60 |doi=10.1007/978-3-031-93227-4_4 |isbn=978-3-031-93227-4|url-access=subscription }}</ref> It is listed on the [[Hong Kong Stock Exchange]] as '''Z.AI Co., Ltd.''', and branded internationally as '''Z.ai'''.

==History==
[[File:Zhipu AI.png|thumb|Logo from 2019 to 2025]]

